# D-FREED-INODE-HOME-NEVER-PUBLISHED-LIVE-CORE-AFTER-CLEAN-UNMOUNT, hypothesis
# H-F6a (the record, session 54), on the one corruption with no verified cause,
# ng0rf1 (2/net/mesh/mpath g2, ino 8388763, nlink 0).  The unlinker's
# inactivation there ran on its BAST worker (kworker/u5:6), not as comm=rm:
# the work serving the peer's EX dropped the unlinker's last reference in its
# trailing xfs_irele, which mxfs_dlm_bast_work_fn runs under its demoter claim
# on purpose.  The inactivation's raw EX acquire sets MXFS_IF_DLM_RELFLUSH, and
# mxfs_dlm_ilock_begin admits a demoter claim while RELFLUSH is set with no
# reload (xfs/xfs_mxfs_ilock.c, "Recursive demoter belt-and-suspenders"), so
# the truncate ran on the dead life's map and its logged live core went home
# over the peer's free.  From the unlink syscall the same ILOCK takes the slow
# path, reloads and adopts the peer's free (P116), which is why every earlier
# H-F6 control lap (57 TCP, 14 CAW peer-freed verdicts, all comm=rm) audited
# CLEAN.  The fix under test is the H-F6 epoch guard already in the build at
# its default (inact_local_epoch_guard=1): an inactivation whose grant was lost
# since the unlink reads the platter before trusting its in-core image, in any
# context.  It has never been exercised in the BAST-worker order.
#
# The order is forced by a test knob new in this build: dbg_bast_lastref_wait_ms
# holds the BAST work's trailing irele of a locally unlinked regular file until
# the work's reference is the last (P-BAST-LASTREF-WAIT, counters
# bast_lastref_waits / bast_lastref_reached).  tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh
# sets it from PLC_LASTREF_WAIT_MS on both nodes with the two delays it always
# sets (setattr 400 ms, live unlink 1000 ms), and reports, for the unlinker,
# bast_ctx_peerfreed (P-INACT-LOCAL-EPOCH verdict=peer-freed lines logged by a
# kworker) and bast_ctx_reloaded (those followed within 1 s by a reload of the
# number, P116-ZOMBIE-ADOPT or P103-RELOAD-REUSE-ADOPT).  Only the guard
# differs between the arms.  Run from ~/src/mxfs-b on the build that carries
# the knob (tools/sibling_sync.sh marker P-BAST-LASTREF-WAIT); the harness
# refuses a node running anything else and reads every knob back.
#
# PREDICTION IF H-F6a IS TRUE: control laps reach (bast_ctx_peerfreed > 0)
# with bast_ctx_reloaded 0 and audit CORRUPT with P-FREE-LIVE-CORE on an inode
# the unlinker's kworker judged peer-freed; fix laps reach and audit CLEAN.
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   PROVEN AND FIXED  at least 2 of the 3 control laps CONTROL-CORRUPT with a
#             P-FREE-LIVE-CORE inode whose unlinker trace (the lap's
#             <A>_audited_inos.txt and <A>_bastctx.txt) shows a
#             verdict=peer-freed comm=kworker line and no reload of it before
#             the audited image was written; and all 3 fix laps PASS (cold
#             audit CLEAN errors=0, no node failure line in either node's
#             stream) with bast_ctx_peerfreed > 0.
#   H-F6a REFUTED  the control laps reach (bast_ctx_peerfreed >= 20 over the
#             three) and either bast_ctx_reloaded equals bast_ctx_peerfreed
#             in every one (the BAST context reloads too), or all three audit
#             CLEAN (the no-reload truncate does not put the core back):
#             ng0rf1 needs another cause.
#   FIX FAILS a fix lap that reached audits CORRUPT or loses a node: attributed
#             from its streams, starting with the guard's own verdict for the
#             audited inode (verdict=ours there means the peer's free was not
#             on the platter when the unlinker's EX was granted).
#   WEAK      reach in every lap but fewer than 2 control laps CORRUPT and not
#             REFUTED: more laps, not a verdict.
#   VACUOUS   bast_ctx_peerfreed 0 on the unlinker (the harness grades it):
#             the injector did not produce the order; the lap measured nothing.
# A lap whose audit is STALE or NONE has no verdict and is rerun.  Any node
# failure line in a control lap is attributed and recorded whatever the audit.
#
# Bound per lap, the sum of the harness's own step bounds, every ssh step
# counted: prep_cluster 300 + srcversion reads 2x20 + knob sets 2x20 + the
# lastref knob set 2x20 + mkdir 30 + workload 40 x (150+1000+1500) ms + 60 =
# 166 + counters 2x40 + knob resets 2x20 + the lastref knob reset 2x20 +
# chk_clean with alloc_witness 150 + stream capture 2x120 = 1166 s.
1170 PLC_LASTREF_WAIT_MS=3000 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh lrc1 0 40 2/net/mesh/mpath g2
1170 PLC_LASTREF_WAIT_MS=3000 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh lrf1 1 40 2/net/mesh/mpath g2
1170 PLC_LASTREF_WAIT_MS=3000 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh lrc2 0 40 2/net/mesh/mpath g2
1170 PLC_LASTREF_WAIT_MS=3000 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh lrf2 1 40 2/net/mesh/mpath g2
1170 PLC_LASTREF_WAIT_MS=3000 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh lrc3 0 40 2/net/mesh/mpath g2
1170 PLC_LASTREF_WAIT_MS=3000 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh lrf3 1 40 2/net/mesh/mpath g2
